ng."]}, "overview": "Sarah Huckabee Sanders seeks a second term as governor in a state that leans about fifteen points Republican, facing Democratic nominee Fredrick Love and a Libertarian candidate. Every major race rating service places the contest in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Sanders roughly a 96-97% chance of winning.\n\nThe one poll on file, an August Hendrix College survey of likely voters, showed a surprisingly narrow five-point Sanders lead, and recent coverage of her welfare-themed campaign ad has drawn criticism from both left and right. Still, with no evidence of a sustained shift and the incumbent's structural advantages, the race remains firmly in Republican hands on paper, with the main question being the size of the margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -11.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0294, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.026, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0419, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0317, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0391, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0223, "margin": -13.0}]}